    <!-- lift_assembly intentionally NOT included here: it is a dynamic (non-static)
         model with a controller plugin, and nesting it inside this static composite
         model would (a) force it static too, since nested models inherit the parent's
         staticness in Gazebo classic, and (b) break the plugin's joint lookups, since
         nested-model plugins load against the outer model with scoped joint names.
         It is included as a top-level sibling model in worlds/restaurant.sdf instead,
         at the same absolute world pose (-10 5.5 0) it would have had here. -->

